# vuln-test-final

Intentionally vulnerable repository for testing the **SecDojo Scanner** with both Rust and C code in a single directory.

> **WARNING:** This code is deliberately insecure. Never use it in production.

---

## Structure

```
vuln-test-final/
├── Cargo.toml          ← Rust project with vulnerable dependencies
├── Cargo.lock          ← Pinned dependency versions (triggers cargo-audit)
├── src/
│   └── main.rs         ← Rust code with unsafe blocks and vulnerable crates
├── vuln.c              ← C code with multiple CWEs
└── README.md           ← This file
```

---

## What the scanner detects

### Rust — cargo-audit (3 findings)

| Severity | Advisory | Crate | Description |
|----------|----------|-------|-------------|
| warning | RUSTSEC-2024-0375 | `atty 0.2.14` | Unmaintained crate |
| warning | RUSTSEC-2024-0320 | `yaml-rust 0.4.4` | Unmaintained crate |
| warning | RUSTSEC-2021-0145 | `atty 0.2.14` | Unsound — potential unaligned read |

### C — Flawfinder (3 findings)

| Severity | CWE | Line | Description |
|----------|-----|------|-------------|
| error | CWE-120 | vuln.c:21 | `strcpy` does not check for buffer overflows |
| error | CWE-134 | vuln.c:43 | Format string can be exploited |
| note | CWE-119/CWE-120 | vuln.c:20 | Statically-sized array may be improperly restricted |

### Not detected (known limitations)

Some vulnerabilities in `vuln.c` are not detected by the current toolchain:

| CWE | Function | Why not detected |
|-----|----------|------------------|
| CWE-416 | `use_after_free()` | Cppcheck needs compilable code; undefined functions in `main()` prevent full analysis |
| CWE-476 | `null_pointer_deref()` | Same reason — `memory_leak()` and `double_free()` are called but not defined |
| CWE-190 | `integer_overflow()` | Not covered by Flawfinder; Cppcheck skips due to compile errors |

---

## How to scan

### From the repo root (inside Docker)

```bash
# Both languages
docker run --rm \
  -v "${PWD}:/workspace" -w /workspace \
  secdojo-scanner:test \
  python3 secdojo/secdojo_scan.py --lang all --path /workspace/examples/vuln-test-final

# Only Rust
docker run --rm \
  -v "${PWD}:/workspace" -w /workspace \
  secdojo-scanner:test \
  python3 secdojo/secdojo_scan.py --lang rust --path /workspace/examples/vuln-test-final

# Only C
docker run --rm \
  -v "${PWD}:/workspace" -w /workspace \
  secdojo-scanner:test \
  python3 secdojo/secdojo_scan.py --lang c --path /workspace/examples/vuln-test-final
```

### Save output to file

```bash
# JSON report
docker run --rm \
  -v "${PWD}:/workspace" -w /workspace \
  secdojo-scanner:test \
  python3 secdojo/secdojo_scan.py --lang all --path /workspace/examples/vuln-test-final --output /workspace/report.json

# Plain text report
docker run --rm \
  -v "${PWD}:/workspace" -w /workspace \
  secdojo-scanner:test \
  python3 secdojo/secdojo_scan.py --lang all --path /workspace/examples/vuln-test-final --output /workspace/report.txt
```

### Local (Windows — example of Rust only, C tools not installed)

```powershell
python secdojo/secdojo_scan.py --lang rust --path examples/vuln-test-final --output report.json
```

